1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,160
Step onto Mars

2
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:02,360
without a suit.

3
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:03,860
Your blood won't boil.

4
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:04,804
Your spit will.

5
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:07,560
Mars does have air.

6
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,560
Less than 1%

7
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:10,260
of the pressure on Earth.

8
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:12,139
And mostly carbon dioxide.

9
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:14,660
Thin air makes water boil

10
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:16,340
at lower temperatures.

11
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:17,280
On Mars,

12
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:19,014
it boils at body temperature.

13
00:00:20,114 --> 00:00:21,680
So why not your blood?

14
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:23,180
Your skin and blood vessels

15
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:24,373
keep it under pressure.

16
00:00:25,373 --> 00:00:25,840
Your tongue

17
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:27,600
is out in the open.

18
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,460
The saliva on it

19
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:29,508
starts to boil.

20
00:00:30,608 --> 00:00:31,700
Don't hold your breath.

21
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,669
That can damage your lungs.

22
00:00:34,669 --> 00:00:35,420
You'd stay awake

23
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,940
for about 10 to 15 seconds.

24
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:38,767
That's how long

25
00:00:38,767 --> 00:00:40,480
oxygen-poor blood takes

26
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:41,758
to reach your brain.

27
00:00:42,858 --> 00:00:43,220
We know,

28
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:44,720
because it happened.

29
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,420
In 1965,

30
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:47,740
a NASA test suit leaked

31
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:49,170
in a vacuum chamber.

32
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:51,040
The man inside

33
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:51,940
stayed conscious

34
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,940
about 14 seconds.

35
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:55,340
His last memory:

36
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,680
the water on his tongue,

37
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:57,893
beginning to boil.

38
00:00:59,093 --> 00:01:00,820
They pumped the air back in.

39
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:01,609
He woke up.

40
00:01:02,709 --> 00:01:04,020
And the cold?

41
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:04,500
Mars averages

42
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,560
minus 59 degrees.

43
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,420
But you wouldn't freeze fast.

44
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:09,903
Heat leaves a body slowly.

45
00:01:11,003 --> 00:01:11,980
So on Mars,

46
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:12,900
keep your blood in,

47
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,275
and your mouth shut.

